---
description: Working in a grok_bot_playground clone
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root first. It is the contract; this rule is only a pointer so it
cannot drift out of sync with it.

- `gb` measures a Grok Bot deployment and proposes Bots as pasteable text. It does not drive the
  Grok Bot app, cannot sign in, and never asks for a credential.
- Route from `gb capabilities --json`. Do not hardcode a verb list or read `bin/`.
- Do not open with `gb triage`; it judges a configured deployment. Start at
  `gb platform --json`, then `gb mirror`.
- Exit 3 means a prerequisite is genuinely missing and the message names it. Corpus verbs
  (`gb corpus`, `gb demand`, `gb findings`, `gb x`) refuse in a clone by design.
- Grok Bot runs on a cloud VM and cannot reach a localhost MCP server. Cursor IDE can. They are
  different products with different config.
